eference-text-cite_note-77&quot;}}"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wik=
i/Sun#cite_note-77" id=3D"mwAzY"><span class=3D"mw-reflink-text" id=3D"mwAz=
c"><span class=3D"cite-bracket" id=3D"mwAzg">[</span>74<span class=3D"cite-=
bracket" id=3D"mwAzk">]</span></span></a></sup> The chromosphere and corona=
 are separated by a thin <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"https://en.wikipedi=
a.org/wiki/Solar_transition_region" title=3D"Solar transition region" id=3D=
"mwAzo">transition region</a> that is frequently considered as an additiona=
l distinct layer.<sup about=3D"#mwt415" class=3D"mw-ref reference" id=3D"ci=
te_ref-78" rel=3D"dc:references" typeof=3D"mw:Extension/ref" data-mw=3D"{&q=
