<p id=3D"mwA1M">The visible surface of the Sun, the photosphere, is the lay=
er below which the Sun becomes <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"https://en.wi=
kipedia.org/wiki/Opaque" title=3D"Opaque" class=3D"mw-redirect" id=3D"mwA1Q=
">opaque</a> to visible light.<sup about=3D"#mwt424" class=3D"mw-ref refere=
nce" id=3D"cite_ref-Abhyankar1977_81-0" rel=3D"dc:references" typeof=3D"mw:=
Extension/ref" data-mw=3D"{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quo=
t;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Abhyankar1977&quot;}}"><a href=3D"https://en.wik=
ipedia.org/wiki/Sun#cite_note-Abhyankar1977-81" id=3D"mwA1U"><span class=3D=
"mw-reflink-text" id=3D"mwA1Y"><span class=3D"cite-bracket" id=3D"mwA1c">[<=
/span>78<span class=3D"cite-bracket" id=3D"mwA1g">]</span></span></a></sup>=
 Photons produced in this layer escape the Sun through the transparent sola=
r atmosphere above it and become solar radiation, sunlight. The change in o=
pacity is due to the decreasing amount of <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"ht=
tps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hydrogen_anion" title=3D"Hydrogen anion" id=3D"=
mwA1k">H<sup id=3D"mwA1o">=E2=88=92</sup> ions</a>, which absorb visible li=
ght easily.<sup about=3D"#mwt425" class=3D"mw-ref reference" id=3D"cite_ref=
-Abhyankar1977_81-1" rel=3D"dc:references" typeof=3D"mw:Extension/ref" data=
-mw=3D"{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot=
;:&quot;Abhyankar1977&quot;}}"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sun=
#cite_note-Abhyankar1977-81" id=3D"mwA1s"><span class=3D"mw-reflink-text" i=
