d=3D"mwA5I">]</span></span></a></sup> It is called the <i id=3D"mwA5M">chro=
mosphere</i> from the Greek root <i id=3D"mwA5Q">chroma</i>, meaning colour=
, because the chromosphere is visible as a coloured flash at the beginning =
and end of total solar eclipses.<sup about=3D"#mwt449" class=3D"mw-ref refe=
rence" id=3D"cite_ref-NASAWorldBook_74-2" rel=3D"dc:references" typeof=3D"m=
