ikipedia.org/wiki/Sun#cite_note-NASAWorldBook-74" id=3D"mwA5U"><span class=
=3D"mw-reflink-text" id=3D"mwA5Y"><span class=3D"cite-bracket" id=3D"mwA5c"=
>[</span>71<span class=3D"cite-bracket" id=3D"mwA5g">]</span></span></a></s=
up> The temperature of the chromosphere increases gradually with altitude, =
ranging up to around 20,000 K near the top.<sup about=3D"#mwt450" class=3D"=
