<p id=3D"mwBHM">The Sun's colour is <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"https://=
en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White" title=3D"White" id=3D"mwBHQ">white</a>, with a=
 <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CIE_1931_colo=
r_space" title=3D"CIE 1931 color space" id=3D"mwBHU">CIE</a> colour-space i=
ndex near (0.3, 0.3), when viewed from space or when the Sun is high in the=
 sky. The Solar radiance per wavelength peaks in the green portion of the s=
pectrum when viewed from space.<sup about=3D"#mwt554" class=3D"mw-ref refer=
ence" id=3D"cite_ref-113" rel=3D"dc:references" typeof=3D"mw:Extension/ref"=
 data-mw=3D"{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;bo=
dy&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-113&quot;}}"><a =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sun#cite_note-113" id=3D"mwBHY"><span=
 class=3D"mw-reflink-text" id=3D"mwBHc"><span class=3D"cite-bracket" id=3D"=
mwBHg">[</span>109<span class=3D"cite-bracket" id=3D"mwBHk">]</span></span>=
</a></sup><sup about=3D"#mwt557" class=3D"mw-ref reference" id=3D"cite_ref-=
114" rel=3D"dc:references" typeof=3D"mw:Extension/ref" data-mw=3D"{&quot;na=
me&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&qu=
ot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-114&quot;}}"><a href=3D"https://en.wi=
kipedia.org/wiki/Sun#cite_note-114" id=3D"mwBHo"><span class=3D"mw-reflink-=
text" id=3D"mwBHs"><span class=3D"cite-bracket" id=3D"mwBHw">[</span>110<sp=
an class=3D"cite-bracket" id=3D"mwBH0">]</span></span></a></sup> When the S=
un is very low in the sky, <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"https://en.wikipe=
dia.org/wiki/Atmospheric_scattering" title=3D"Atmospheric scattering" class=
=3D"mw-redirect" id=3D"mwBH4">atmospheric scattering</a> renders the Sun ye=
llow, red, orange, or magenta, and in rare occasions even <a rel=3D"mw:Wiki=
Link" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green_flash" title=3D"Green fla=
sh" id=3D"mwBH8">green or blue</a>. Some cultures mentally picture the Sun =
as yellow and some even red; the cultural reasons for this are debated.<sup=
 about=3D"#mwt560" class=3D"mw-ref reference" id=3D"cite_ref-yellow_sun_par=
adox_115-0" rel=3D"dc:references" typeof=3D"mw:Extension/ref" data-mw=3D"{&=
quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;y=
ellow sun paradox&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-referenc=
e-text-cite_note-yellow_sun_paradox-115&quot;}}"><a href=3D"https://en.wiki=
pedia.org/wiki/Sun#cite_note-yellow_sun_paradox-115" id=3D"mwBIA"><span cla=
ss=3D"mw-reflink-text" id=3D"mwBIE"><span class=3D"cite-bracket" id=3D"mwBI=
I">[</span>111<span class=3D"cite-bracket" id=3D"mwBIM">]</span></span></a>=
</sup></p>

<p id=3D"mwBIQ">An <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/=
wiki/Optical_phenomenon" title=3D"Optical phenomenon" id=3D"mwBIU">optical =
phenomenon</a>, known as a <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"https://en.wikipe=
dia.org/wiki/Green_flash" title=3D"Green flash" id=3D"mwBIY">green flash</a=
>, can sometimes be seen shortly after sunset or before sunrise. The flash =
is caused by light from the Sun just below the horizon being <a rel=3D"mw:W=
ikiLink" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Refraction" title=3D"Refract=
ion" id=3D"mwBIc">bent</a> (usually through a <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=
=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Temperature_inversion" title=3D"Temperatu=
re inversion" class=3D"mw-redirect" id=3D"mwBIg">temperature inversion</a>)=
 towards the observer. Light of shorter wavelengths (violet, blue, green) i=
s bent more than that of longer wavelengths (yellow, orange, red) but the v=
iolet and blue light is <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia=
.org/wiki/Rayleigh_scattering" title=3D"Rayleigh scattering" id=3D"mwBIk">s=
cattered</a> more, leaving light that is perceived as green.<sup about=3D"#=
mwt563" class=3D"mw-ref reference" id=3D"cite_ref-116" rel=3D"dc:references=
" typeof=3D"mw:Extension/ref" data-mw=3D"{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,=
&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-te=
xt-cite_note-116&quot;}}"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sun#cite=
_note-116" id=3D"mwBIo"><span class=3D"mw-reflink-text" id=3D"mwBIs"><span =
class=3D"cite-bracket" id=3D"mwBIw">[</span>112<span class=3D"cite-bracket"=
 id=3D"mwBI0">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

