<p id=3D"mwBRI">The solar magnetic field extends well beyond the Sun itself=
. The electrically conducting solar wind plasma carries the Sun's magnetic =
field into space, forming what is called the <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D=
"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Interplanetary_magnetic_field" title=3D"Inte=
rplanetary magnetic field" id=3D"mwBRM">interplanetary magnetic field</a>.<=
sup about=3D"#mwt624" class=3D"mw-ref reference" id=3D"cite_ref-Russell2001=
_90-2" rel=3D"dc:references" typeof=3D"mw:Extension/ref" data-mw=3D"{&quot;=
name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Russel=
l2001&quot;}}"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sun#cite_note-Russe=
ll2001-90" id=3D"mwBRQ"><span class=3D"mw-reflink-text" id=3D"mwBRU"><span =
class=3D"cite-bracket" id=3D"mwBRY">[</span>86<span class=3D"cite-bracket" =
id=3D"mwBRc">]</span></span></a></sup> In an approximation known as <i id=
=3D"mwBRg"><a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ide=
al_magnetohydrodynamics" title=3D"Ideal magnetohydrodynamics" class=3D"mw-r=
edirect" id=3D"mwBRk">ideal magnetohydrodynamics</a></i>, plasma only moves=
 along magnetic field lines. As a result, the outward-flowing solar wind st=
retches the interplanetary magnetic field outward, forcing it into a roughl=
y radial structure. For a simple dipolar solar magnetic field, with opposit=
e hemispherical polarities on either side of the solar magnetic equator, a =
thin <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heliosphe=
ric_current_sheet" title=3D"Heliospheric current sheet" id=3D"mwBRo">curren=
t sheet</a> is formed in the solar wind. At great distances, the rotation o=
f the Sun twists the dipolar magnetic field and corresponding current sheet=
 into an <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Archi=
medean_spiral" title=3D"Archimedean spiral" id=3D"mwBRs">Archimedean spiral=
</a> structure called the <i id=3D"mwBRw"><a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"ht=
tps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parker_spiral" title=3D"Parker spiral" class=3D=
"mw-redirect" id=3D"mwBR0">Parker spiral</a></i>.<sup about=3D"#mwt625" cla=
ss=3D"mw-ref reference" id=3D"cite_ref-Russell2001_90-3" rel=3D"dc:referenc=
es" typeof=3D"mw:Extension/ref" data-mw=3D"{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot=
;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Russell2001&quot;}}"><a href=3D=
"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sun#cite_note-Russell2001-90" id=3D"mwBR4"><=
span class=3D"mw-reflink-text" id=3D"mwBR8"><span class=3D"cite-bracket" id=
=3D"mwBSA">[</span>86<span class=3D"cite-bracket" id=3D"mwBSE">]</span></sp=
an></a></sup></p>

