figcaption></figure>

<p id=3D"mwBU8">The Sun's magnetic field leads to many effects that are col=
lectively called <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wi=
ki/Solar_variation" title=3D"Solar variation" class=3D"mw-redirect" id=3D"m=
wBVA">solar activity</a>. <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"https://en.wikiped=
ia.org/wiki/Solar_flares" title=3D"Solar flares" class=3D"mw-redirect" id=
=3D"mwBVE">Solar flares</a> and <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"https://en.w=
ikipedia.org/wiki/Coronal_mass_ejections" title=3D"Coronal mass ejections" =
class=3D"mw-redirect" id=3D"mwBVI">coronal mass ejections</a> tend to occur=
 at sunspot groups. Slowly changing high-speed streams of solar wind are em=
itted from <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cor=
onal_holes" title=3D"Coronal holes" class=3D"mw-redirect" id=3D"mwBVM">coro=
nal holes</a> at the photospheric surface. Both coronal mass ejections and =
high-speed streams of solar wind carry plasma and the interplanetary magnet=
ic field outward into the Solar System.<sup about=3D"#mwt647" class=3D"mw-r=
ef reference" id=3D"cite_ref-Zirker2002_140-0" rel=3D"dc:references" typeof=
=3D"mw:Extension/ref" data-mw=3D"{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;at=
trs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Zirker2002&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot=
;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-Zirker2002-140&quot;}}"><a href=
=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sun#cite_note-Zirker2002-140" id=3D"mwBVQ=
"><span class=3D"mw-reflink-text" id=3D"mwBVU"><span class=3D"cite-bracket"=
 id=3D"mwBVY">[</span>136<span class=3D"cite-bracket" id=3D"mwBVc">]</span>=
</span></a></sup> The effects of solar activity on Earth include <a rel=3D"=
mw:WikiLink" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Auroras" title=3D"Aurora=
s" class=3D"mw-redirect" id=3D"mwBVg">auroras</a> at moderate to high latit=
udes and the disruption of radio communications and <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electric_power" title=3D"Electric pow=
er" id=3D"mwBVk">electric power</a>. Solar activity is thought to have play=
ed a large role in the <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.=
org/wiki/Formation_and_evolution_of_the_Solar_System" title=3D"Formation an=
d evolution of the Solar System" id=3D"mwBVo">formation and evolution of th=
e Solar System</a>.<sup about=3D"#mwt650" class=3D"mw-ref reference" id=3D"=
