</div>

<p id=3D"mwBXk">The temperature of the photosphere is approximately 6,000<s=
pan typeof=3D"mw:Entity" id=3D"mwBXo">&nbsp;</span>K, whereas the temperatu=
re of the corona reaches <span class=3D"nowrap" about=3D"#mwt667" typeof=3D=
"mw:Transclusion" id=3D"mwBXs" data-mw=3D"{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;templa=
te&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;val&quot;,&quot;href&quo=
t;:&quot;./Template:Val&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&=
quot;:&quot;1000000&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;-&quot;},&qu=
ot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2000000&quot;},&quot;u&quot;:{&quot;wt&quo=
t;:&quot;K&quot;},&quot;fmt&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;commas&quot;}},&quo=
t;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span data-sort-value=3D"7006100000000000000=E2=99=A0"></s=
pan>1,000,000=E2=80=932,000,000<span typeof=3D"mw:Entity">&nbsp;</span>K</s=
pan>.<sup about=3D"#mwt668" class=3D"mw-ref reference" id=3D"cite_ref-Erdel=
yi2007_87-3" rel=3D"dc:references" typeof=3D"mw:Extension/ref" data-mw=3D"{=
&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;=
Erdelyi2007&quot;}}"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sun#cite_note=
-Erdelyi2007-87" id=3D"mwBXw"><span class=3D"mw-reflink-text" id=3D"mwBX0">=
<span class=3D"cite-bracket" id=3D"mwBX4">[</span>84<span class=3D"cite-bra=
cket" id=3D"mwBX8">]</span></span></a></sup> The high temperature of the co=
rona shows that it is heated by something other than direct <a rel=3D"mw:Wi=
kiLink" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heat_conduction" title=3D"Hea=
t conduction" class=3D"mw-redirect" id=3D"mwBYA">heat conduction</a> from t=
he photosphere.<sup about=3D"#mwt669" class=3D"mw-ref reference" id=3D"cite=
_ref-Russell2001_90-4" rel=3D"dc:references" typeof=3D"mw:Extension/ref" da=
ta-mw=3D"{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&qu=
ot;:&quot;Russell2001&quot;}}"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sun=
#cite_note-Russell2001-90" id=3D"mwBYE"><span class=3D"mw-reflink-text" id=
=3D"mwBYI"><span class=3D"cite-bracket" id=3D"mwBYM">[</span>86<span class=
=3D"cite-bracket" id=3D"mwBYQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id=3D"mwBYU">It is thought that the energy necessary to heat the corona =
is provided by turbulent motion in the convection zone below the photospher=
e, and two main mechanisms have been proposed to explain coronal heating.<s=
up about=3D"#mwt670" class=3D"mw-ref reference" id=3D"cite_ref-Erdelyi2007_=
87-4" rel=3D"dc:references" typeof=3D"mw:Extension/ref" data-mw=3D"{&quot;n=
ame&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Erdelyi=
2007&quot;}}"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sun#cite_note-Erdely=
i2007-87" id=3D"mwBYY"><span class=3D"mw-reflink-text" id=3D"mwBYc"><span c=
lass=3D"cite-bracket" id=3D"mwBYg">[</span>84<span class=3D"cite-bracket" i=
d=3D"mwBYk">]</span></span></a></sup> The first is wave heating, in which s=
ound, gravitational or magnetohydrodynamic waves are produced by turbulence=
 in the convection zone.<sup about=3D"#mwt671" class=3D"mw-ref reference" i=
d=3D"cite_ref-Erdelyi2007_87-5" rel=3D"dc:references" typeof=3D"mw:Extensio=
n/ref" data-mw=3D"{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quo=
t;name&quot;:&quot;Erdelyi2007&quot;}}"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org=
/wiki/Sun#cite_note-Erdelyi2007-87" id=3D"mwBYo"><span class=3D"mw-reflink-=
text" id=3D"mwBYs"><span class=3D"cite-bracket" id=3D"mwBYw">[</span>84<spa=
n class=3D"cite-bracket" id=3D"mwBY0">]</span></span></a></sup> These waves=
 travel upward and dissipate in the corona, depositing their energy in the =
ambient matter in the form of heat.<sup about=3D"#mwt674" class=3D"mw-ref r=
eference" id=3D"cite_ref-Alfven_146-0" rel=3D"dc:references" typeof=3D"mw:E=
xtension/ref" data-mw=3D"{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot=
;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Alfven&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&q=
uot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-Alfven-146&quot;}}"><a href=3D"https://en.w=
ikipedia.org/wiki/Sun#cite_note-Alfven-146" id=3D"mwBY4"><span class=3D"mw-=
reflink-text" id=3D"mwBY8"><span class=3D"cite-bracket" id=3D"mwBZA">[</spa=
n>142<span class=3D"cite-bracket" id=3D"mwBZE">]</span></span></a></sup> Th=
e other is magnetic heating, in which magnetic energy is continuously built=
 up by photospheric motion and released through <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=
=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magnetic_reconnection" title=3D"Magnetic =
reconnection" id=3D"mwBZI">magnetic reconnection</a> in the form of large s=
olar flares and myriad similar but smaller events=E2=80=94<a rel=3D"mw:Wiki=
Link" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nanoflares" title=3D"Nanoflares=
" class=3D"mw-redirect" id=3D"mwBZM">nanoflares</a>.<sup about=3D"#mwt677" =
class=3D"mw-ref reference" id=3D"cite_ref-Parker2_147-0" rel=3D"dc:referenc=
es" typeof=3D"mw:Extension/ref" data-mw=3D"{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot=
;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Parker2&quot;},&quot;body&quot;=
:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-Parker2-147&quot;}}"><a =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sun#cite_note-Parker2-147" id=3D"mwBZ=
Q"><span class=3D"mw-reflink-text" id=3D"mwBZU"><span class=3D"cite-bracket=
" id=3D"mwBZY">[</span>143<span class=3D"cite-bracket" id=3D"mwBZc">]</span=
></span></a></sup></p>

<p id=3D"mwBZg">Currently, it is unclear whether waves are an efficient hea=
ting mechanism. All waves except Alfv=C3=A9n waves have been found to dissi=
pate or refract before reaching the corona.<sup about=3D"#mwt680" class=3D"=
mw-ref reference" id=3D"cite_ref-Sturrock_148-0" rel=3D"dc:references" type=
of=3D"mw:Extension/ref" data-mw=3D"{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;=
attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Sturrock&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot=
;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-Sturrock-148&quot;}}"><a href=
=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sun#cite_note-Sturrock-148" id=3D"mwBZk">=
<span class=3D"mw-reflink-text" id=3D"mwBZo"><span class=3D"cite-bracket" i=
d=3D"mwBZs">[</span>144<span class=3D"cite-bracket" id=3D"mwBZw">]</span></=
span></a></sup> In addition, Alfv=C3=A9n waves do not easily dissipate in t=
he corona. The current research focus has therefore shifted toward flare he=
ating mechanisms.<sup about=3D"#mwt681" class=3D"mw-ref reference" id=3D"ci=
te_ref-Erdelyi2007_87-6" rel=3D"dc:references" typeof=3D"mw:Extension/ref" =
data-mw=3D"{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&=
quot;:&quot;Erdelyi2007&quot;}}"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/S=
un#cite_note-Erdelyi2007-87" id=3D"mwBZ0"><span class=3D"mw-reflink-text" i=
d=3D"mwBZ4"><span class=3D"cite-bracket" id=3D"mwBZ8">[</span>84<span class=
=3D"cite-bracket" id=3D"mwBaA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

