ence-text-cite_note-179&quot;}}"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/S=
un#cite_note-179" id=3D"mwBtk"><span class=3D"mw-reflink-text" id=3D"mwBto"=
><span class=3D"cite-bracket" id=3D"mwBts">[</span>175<span class=3D"cite-b=
racket" id=3D"mwBtw">]</span></span></a></sup> The orbits of the inner plan=
ets, including of the Earth, are similarly displaced by the same gravitatio=
nal forces, so the movement of the Sun has little effect on the relative po=
sitions of the Earth and the Sun or on solar irradiance on the Earth as a f=
unction of time.<sup about=3D"#mwt809" class=3D"mw-ref reference" id=3D"cit=
e_ref-180" rel=3D"dc:references" typeof=3D"mw:Extension/ref" data-mw=3D"{&q=
