n>214<span class=3D"cite-bracket" id=3D"mwB_k">]</span></span></a></sup></p=
>

<p id=3D"mwB_o">The first reasonably accurate distance to the Sun was deter=
mined in 1684 by <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wi=
ki/Giovanni_Domenico_Cassini" title=3D"Giovanni Domenico Cassini" id=3D"mwB=
_s">Giovanni Domenico Cassini</a>. Knowing that direct measurements of the =
solar parallax were difficult, he chose to measure the Martian parallax. Ha=
ving sent <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jean=
_Richer" title=3D"Jean Richer" id=3D"mwB_w">Jean Richer</a> to <a rel=3D"mw=
:WikiLink" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cayenne" title=3D"Cayenne"=
 id=3D"mwB_0">Cayenne</a>, part of <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"https://e=
n.wikipedia.org/wiki/French_Guiana" title=3D"French Guiana" id=3D"mwB_4">Fr=
ench Guiana</a>, for simultaneous measurements, Cassini in Paris determined=
 the parallax of <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wi=
ki/Mars" title=3D"Mars" id=3D"mwB_8">Mars</a> when Mars was at its closest =
to Earth in 1672. Using the circumference distance between the two observat=
ions, Cassini calculated the Earth=E2=80=93Mars distance, then used <a rel=
=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kepler's_laws" title=
=3D"Kepler's laws" class=3D"mw-redirect" id=3D"mwCAA">Kepler's laws</a> to =
determine the Earth=E2=80=93Sun distance. His value, about 10% smaller than=
 modern values, was much larger than all previous estimates.<sup about=3D"#=
mwt969" class=3D"mw-ref reference" id=3D"cite_ref-219" rel=3D"dc:references=
" typeof=3D"mw:Extension/ref" data-mw=3D"{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,=
&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-te=
xt-cite_note-219&quot;}}"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sun#cite=
_note-219" id=3D"mwCAE"><span class=3D"mw-reflink-text" id=3D"mwCAI"><span =
class=3D"cite-bracket" id=3D"mwCAM">[</span>215<span class=3D"cite-bracket"=
 id=3D"mwCAQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id=3D"mwCAU">From an observation of a <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"htt=
ps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Transit_of_Venus" title=3D"Transit of Venus" id=
