<p id=3D"mwCB4">In 1666, <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"https://en.wikipedi=
a.org/wiki/Isaac_Newton" title=3D"Isaac Newton" id=3D"mwCB8">Isaac Newton</=
a> observed the Sun's light using a <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"https://=
en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prism_(optics)" title=3D"Prism (optics)" id=3D"mwCCA"=
>prism</a>, and showed that it is made up of light of many colours.<sup abo=
ut=3D"#mwt982" class=3D"mw-ref reference" id=3D"cite_ref-223" rel=3D"dc:ref=
erences" typeof=3D"mw:Extension/ref" data-mw=3D"{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref=
&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-refer=
ence-text-cite_note-223&quot;}}"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/S=
un#cite_note-223" id=3D"mwCCE"><span class=3D"mw-reflink-text" id=3D"mwCCI"=
><span class=3D"cite-bracket" id=3D"mwCCM">[</span>219<span class=3D"cite-b=
racket" id=3D"mwCCQ">]</span></span></a></sup> In 1800, <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLi=
nk" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Herschel" title=3D"Willia=
m Herschel" id=3D"mwCCU">William Herschel</a> discovered <a rel=3D"mw:WikiL=
ink" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Infrared" title=3D"Infrared" id=
=3D"mwCCY">infrared</a> radiation beyond the red part of the solar spectrum=
.<sup about=3D"#mwt985" class=3D"mw-ref reference" id=3D"cite_ref-224" rel=
=3D"dc:references" typeof=3D"mw:Extension/ref" data-mw=3D"{&quot;name&quot;=
:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quo=
t;mw-reference-text-cite_note-224&quot;}}"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.=
org/wiki/Sun#cite_note-224" id=3D"mwCCc"><span class=3D"mw-reflink-text" id=
=3D"mwCCg"><span class=3D"cite-bracket" id=3D"mwCCk">[</span>220<span class=
=3D"cite-bracket" id=3D"mwCCo">]</span></span></a></sup> The 19th century s=
